# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Intelli-Credit environment variables
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# All keys are SERVER-SIDE ONLY. The client never sees them — every
# Gemini / bureau call goes through the /api/analyze serverless function.
#
# LOCAL DEV:
#   Copy this file to `.env` and fill in the values, then `npm run dev`.
#   (server.ts loads .env via dotenv and exposes these to the dev
#   /api/analyze route.)
#
# VERCEL DEPLOYMENT:
#   In your Vercel project go to Settings → Environment Variables and add
#   each value below (no VITE_ prefix). They are injected at runtime into
#   the serverless function and never reach the browser bundle.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Google Gemini API key — REQUIRED for document analysis to work.
# Get one at https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
GEMINI_API_KEY=

# Optional: eCourts integration key, read by api/_lib/mcp-tools.ts
# (the search_cases tool). When unset, that tool returns a helpful error.
ECOURTS_API_KEY=
